  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The Global Horizon (2021), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 15 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 1,019 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The Global Horizon by Knut Graw and Samuli Schielke was published by Leuven University Press in 2021. Conceptually, the work connects to Globalization, Sociocultural evolution, Ethnography, Focus (optics) and Sociology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 15 citations. Notable citing venues include Africa, Emotion, space and society and Sa\u00fade e Sociedade. The citing works include 12 journal articles, 2 book chapters and 1 report. They come from 10 countries, led by Italy, the United States and Canada.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 1,019 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Reduced inequalities among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>",
  "events": {},
  "scite": {},
  "story_type": "BookStory",
